{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model systematically underpredicts the level by ~2–5 €/t across most horizons, especially during rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift (larger when recent trend is positive).",
    "Trend/lag error: forecasts react too slowly to upswings (and slightly to downswings), producing a lagged path. Increase sensitivity to the last 5–10 day slope; if slope > 0, add a positive ramp that grows with horizon.",
    "Underestimation of volatility and upside tails: true outcomes show larger upward moves than forecast (missed rallies). Inflate forecast dispersion and allow higher highs when recent realized vol is elevated.",
    "Excess mean-reversion: model pulls prices back toward mid-60s even when regime shifts to upper-60s/near-70. Reduce mean-reversion strength when price breaks above recent 20–30d range or when momentum is positive.",
    "Horizon-specific bias: error tends to accumulate with horizon (days 10–25 most underpredicted in examples). Use a horizon-dependent additive correction that increases out to ~3–4 weeks, then flattens."
  ]
}
